<div><head n="1.">Introduction</head><p>Müller and Ångström report <ref type="bibr" target="#b0 #b1">(Smith 2020; Jones 2021)</ref> and <ref type="bibr" target="#b9">(Missing 1999)</ref> and <ref type="bibr" target="">(Empty 2000)</ref>.<ref type="foot" target="#foot_0">1</ref> We saw (Twice) and <ref type="bibr" target="#b1">(Twice)</ref> again.</p><p>See <ref type="formula" target="#formula_0">(1)</ref>, <ref type="other" target="#x">this</ref>, <ref target="#y">that</ref> and <ref type="figure" target="#fig_0">Fig. 3</ref>, <ref type="figure" target="#fig_1">Figure 4</ref>, <ref type="table" target="#tab_0">Table 1a</ref> and <ref type="table" target="#tab_1">Table 2</ref>.</p></div>
<div><head>Results</head><p>We found t(20) &lt;&gt; 2.10 and r ≤= .5, p =&lt; .05 and F(1, 2) == 3.</p><p>Data are on <ref type="url" target="https://osf.io/xyz">the OSF page</ref> and at <ref type="url" target="https://osf.io/abc">https://osf.io/abc</ref>, which is https://osf.io/abc.</p></div>
